cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Who Judges the Judges? Stakeholder-defined evaluation of candidate base models for a student wellbeing signposting chatbot"
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Noori
    given-names: Jawad
    affiliation: "School of Computer Science, University of Nottingham"
year: 2026
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  An accessibility screen applied to 31 LLM evaluation tools, a stakeholder-derived
  evaluation blueprint of 11 scenarios and 74 criteria for a university student
  wellbeing signposting chatbot, and results for four candidate base models scored
  by a dual cross-provider LLM judge panel. Reports a safety pattern in the models
  and an under-surfaced reliability problem in the evaluation itself.
keywords:
  - AI assurance
  - LLM evaluation
  - mental health
  - LLM-as-judge
  - inter-rater reliability
